cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, models or results, please cite it as below."
title: "Consistency by Construction: Cross-Encoders with Reversal-Aware Decoding for SemEval-2027 Task 2 (DiCo-NLI)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Le"
    given-names: "Duc Minh"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MinLee0210/dico-nli-challenge"
keywords:
  - natural language inference
  - directional consistency
  - cross-encoder
  - multilingual
  - Basque
  - SemEval-2027
abstract: >-
  A config-driven system for SemEval-2027 Task 2 (DiCo-NLI): multilingual
  cross-encoders with consistency-aware decoding that pools the
  log-probabilities of a phrase pair, its reversed twin and its language views
  in one canonical frame, guaranteeing reversal consistency for every pair
  predicted as reversible. Includes an exactly reversal-equivariant model
  option, ensembling tools, a study of NEGATIVE_OTHER detection, and a
  technical report.
